r"""patch_L494_1_info_note_and_find_20261026.py -- the i button's note and Find a body
(L-494, L-493), Oct 26.

Built on gallery dae4a7cdd67db869ad473b20068bd553aeabd1e5 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io (branch
main), with orrery 8f4173c4cb28abfdac622b54ed33031e169f6c66 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery.

WHAT IT DOES, all or nothing

    L-494, Tony's option C from the Design canvas: no text box ends with
    "For more information and references please click on the info "i"
    button top right." any more, in any room. Instead a first visit is
    greeted by a small note under the i button, "More information and
    the sources for everything you see are here.", with a Got it button.
    Got it, or tapping the i button, puts it away for good in that
    browser.

    L-493: the Solar System room's drawer has a search box, "Find a
    body". It matches any of a body's names -- the drawer's, the
    orrery's, JPL's (so "atlas" finds the ATLAS comets) and the Horizons
    id -- ignoring capitals, spaces and punctuation. Matching groups open
    and say "1 of 10 shown"; a row found by JPL's name says so. The x
    button or Reset clears it.

WHAT IT EDITS

    interactive.html: the note, the search box, the change note.
    gallery/solar_system_drawer.js: the search rules and their words.
    gallery/feature_renderers.js, gallery/earth_geometry.js: the old
        sentence is no longer added to any text box.
    tools/mirror_objects.py, tools/test_mirror_objects.py: the mirror
        copies JPL's name for each body from the orrery's export.
    data/objects_config.json: JPL's name on each linked body, as the
        mirror writes it.
    documentation/: the checks for all of the above, and the hover
        record re-written as fixture_hovers_L494_on_dae4a7cd.json, which
        differs from the last one only by that sentence, on 44 hovers.
    tools/headless/walk_solar_system_drawer.js: Claude's room walk.

    No cache change, so no build is needed: it reaches a visitor on the
    push.

HOW TO RUN

    Save it in the website folder (tonyquintanilla.github.io), open it
    in VS Code and press Run. It prints an "ok" line per file and "patch
    applied"; a second run refuses. Then gallery_maintenance_run.py,
    which should be green; move this file into documentation\, commit
    and push. Undo before a commit is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop.

Written October 26, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""
